-- title:
--   Prime-to-p abelian quotient family for the level-N₀p Néron object
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ nonzero, $p$ prime and nonzero, and $p \nmid N_0$; fix a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ lying over $p$, meaning that $p$ is a nonunit of $A$; fix level data $\Lambda$ for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying the predicate `IsJacobian` (so that $\Lambda.f$ carries an abelian-scheme property bundle, its relative group law is commutative and compatible with the identifications $\Lambda$ gives of $J_0(N_0)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with sections over the generic point and of the corresponding residue-field Picard group with sections over the special point, is Galois-equivariant, compatible with reduction mod the place of $A$ where applicable, and carries an action of the Hecke algebra realised by endomorphisms of $\Lambda.f$); and fix an object $O$ of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, i.e. a smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective group scheme with preconnected fibres over the base of $p$, with a group law, an identification of $J_0(N_0p)$ with its generic-fibre sections compatible with addition, the Galois action and the Hecke action, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, properness of its generic fibre, and the further toric data. Then there exists a single family of additive maps $\mathrm{abq}(m,hm)\colon O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m \to J_0(N_0)\times J_0(N_0)$, indexed by the natural numbers $m$ coprime to $p$, where $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ is the subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated $O$-point extends to the place of $A$, such that: (i) $\mathrm{abq}(m,hm)\,x=0$ if and only if $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ (trivial for $m=0$); (ii) the range of $\mathrm{abq}(m,hm)$ is exactly the $m$-torsion subgroup of $J_0(N_0)\times J_0(N_0)$; (iii) the maps are compatible under $m \mid m'$, for $m,m'$ coprime to $p$, on points of $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ that also lie in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m'$; (iv) for every prime $\ell \nmid N_0p$ and every $x$ in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ with $\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell \cdot x$ again in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ (actions via `heckeModuleBar` at levels $N_0p$ and $N_0$), $\mathrm{abq}$ of $\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell \cdot x$ is the componentwise $\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell$-translate of $\mathrm{abq}(m,hm)\,x$; and (v) for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ and every $x$ with $\sigma \cdot x$ again in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, $\mathrm{abq}$ of $\sigma \cdot x$ is the componentwise $\sigma$-translate of $\mathrm{abq}(m,hm)\,x$.
--
--   This packages, for the Jacobian of $X_0(N_0p)$ at a place above $p$, the description of the prime-to-$p$ torsion of the finite part of the Néron object modulo its toric part as the $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0)^2$, equivariantly for the Hecke operators away from $N_0p$ and for the decomposition group at $A$; this is the group-theoretic input underlying the Deligne–Rapoport description of the special fibre used in Ribet's level-lowering argument. It is used to produce the corresponding data bundle in [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_toric_eq_fin_eq_of_forall_smul_sub_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_toric_eq_fin_eq_of_forall_smul_sub_mem).
